# Round q35oracle: ik's CPU node dumps of the Qwen3.6-35B-A3B Q4_K_M file (21,166,757,728 B), each one
# `just dump-ref-qwen35moe [VARIANT]` under this card: the batch set, then step4-every-node, d1k,
# u1s4-every-node and u1s5-every-node, one lease each.
# Minutes per dump [derived, round q35oracle phase 1]:
#   page-in  the file read cold once: 0.1 % resident at 09:16 KST (mincore); 21.17 GB at 1.07-1.33 GB/s,
#            the single-stream populate rates of the 09-13 and 09-23 witnesses: 16-20 s, the first dump
#            only, again on a later one if a peer's host load evicts the file
#   fixed    lease, witnesses, load from the page cache and context: 9-21 s — the V4.1 d1 dump's
#            witness window was 14 s around a 6.5 s prefill and a 1.6 s step (no populate, --defer-experts);
#            18.4 s lay between qwen3moe's batch manifest and its step4 set's first file (09-24, 18.6 GB warm)
#   prefill  step sets of 4-5 tokens < 1 s; d1k's fused 1,024 tokens 2.5-6 s (qwen3moe d4k: 4,096 in
#            about 14 s from the same mtimes, scaled by the active-weight ratio 2.44 / 2.73 B)
#   dump     1.3-1.9 GB a set, 22 state-sized files of 2 MiB per GDN layer x 30, at the 0.5 GB/s the
#            qwen3moe d1k and d4k step dumps wrote: 3-4 s
#   batch 0.5-0.8 min cold; step4, u1s4, u1s5 0.2-0.5 min; d1k 0.3-0.5 min; 1.5-2.8 min in all
kind: exclusive
reason: dump_ref runs ik on 32 CPU threads and pages the 21.2 GB file into the page cache; beside a
  timed run or a gate batch it would take their cores and their memory bandwidth, so it holds the lease;
  why now: the qwen35moe oracle every Qwen3.6 kernel and body round is judged against (round q35oracle)
minutes: 0.2..1.2
# Measured (2026-09-27, 00:27:41-00:28:39 UTC, loadavg 28-37 beside a peer batch): batch 23 s, step4 8 s,
# d1k 12 s, u1s4 7 s, u1s5 8 s — 58 s in all against 1.5-2.8 min. The missed term is `fixed`: about 3 s
# (8 - 3.9 dump - 1.2 prefill), not 9-21 s — the 18.4 s mtime gap it came from held a box.sh round trip
# between two separate commands. dump 3.9-4.4 s, d1k prefill 4.0 s and the five set sizes fell inside their bands.
